# Hooks and shell scripts stay LF: Git for Windows defaults to autocrlf=true, and a CRLF shebang
# makes Git Bash fail with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M". Scoped narrowly so no other file
# is renormalized.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# A file a script or tool writes is marked linguist-generated here, and another project's text
# linguist-vendored, so the Size cap skips it (size-cap/size-cap.mjs); every file was written by
# hand on 2026-11-04, so none is.
